+# Local Microsoft PC configuration and build
+
+Base upstream commit: `fc3535868935c16b7260be0d5749c0d84b2a9b1a` (2025-10-06). The public release remains 1.0.12.9; this is a local source build with that assembly version, not a new official release.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `MainWindowViewModel.cs`: export runs on `RxApp.MainThreadScheduler`. The original task-pool scheduler caused a WPF collection-thread exception after export. The patched export completes, shows its success message, keeps controls enabled, and writes the active Microsoft cached order.
+- `GUI.csproj` and API call sites: SharpCompress upgraded from 0.39.0 to 0.48.0. NuGet reported GHSA-6c8g-7p36-r338 against the old version. Updated encoding, BZip2 stream, archive factory and writer factory calls to the new API.
+- Core/GUI project files: optional `BG3MMReleaseLibraries` property reuses LSLib and CrossSpeak from the official 1.0.12.9 archive. Normal upstream references remain when the property is absent.
+
+No game executable modifications. The directory layout is handled by settings and two junctions in `ManagerView`; the launcher uses the Microsoft package AUMID through Explorer. This avoids Steam launch assumptions.
+
+## Build
+
+Private Microsoft .NET SDK 8.0.425 and Windows Desktop runtime 8.0.31 are under `Tools/DotNet` in the parent modding workspace. Archive hashes and official source URLs are recorded in `Logs/ToolRuntimeSources.json` and `ToolsInventory.json`.
+
+```powershell
+$work = 'C:\BG3Build'
+& "$work\Tools\DotNet\dotnet.exe" build "$work\Source\BG3ModManager\src\GUI\GUI.csproj" -c Release -p:Platform=x64 -p:SolutionDir="$work\Source\BG3ModManager\" -p:BG3MMReleaseLibraries="$work\Tools\BG3ModManager\_Lib" -p:OutputPath="$work\Build\BG3ModManager\" --nologo
+```
+
+Use this build command, not the repository's publishing scripts. Build: zero errors; eight existing warnings. Runtime: active/inactive movement, successful live export and Microsoft package launch verified. Exported XML survived game startup byte-for-byte (`Logs/BG3MM-LiveExport.lsx`, `Logs/BG3MM-AfterLaunch.lsx`).
+
+The log's missing Larian launcher preferences and empty synthetic profile UUID warnings are expected for this directory view. They did not prevent export. Xbox manages the signed-in profile; BG3MM manages only packages and cached order here.
+
+Keep this build until an upstream release incorporates equivalent fixes; a manager auto-update could replace it. Source diff, original binaries, build log and deployed hashes remain in the parent workspace.
